<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna: hoisting a shared if/else suffix must not free a block a goto still
    names.  dedupitetail moves the statement both arms end with to after the
    if.  When that leaves an arm with one component, the arm's list is
    unwrapped and freed.  Here a goto from the else arm targets the whole true
    arm, so the goto kept the freed list's id, and printing its label panicked
    (substrate/block.rs "invalid SlotMap key used"; Ghidra 12.1.2's
    llio_i386.dll sub_10001fee hit it).  The goto now names the arm's sole
    component, which starts at the same statement and prints the same label.

    Stage / sub-stage: P8 structure, goto-quality
    (p8_structure/kuna_dedupitetail.rs, BlockGraph::kuna_hoist_ite_suffix).
    Two passes: option dedupitetail off keeps one shared(y) per arm, and the
    default hoists it to one copy after the if.  No option gates the fix; before
    it the second pass panicked.

    Hand-assembled x86-64 (as -64, bytes verbatim):

        g:        push rbx; mov ebx,esi; cmp edi,1; je else_arm
        true_arm: call cond_a; test eax,eax; je t_shared; call body_a
        t_shared: mov edi,ebx; call shared; jmp conv
        else_arm: call cond_b; test eax,eax; je e_shared
                  call cond_c; test eax,eax; jne true_arm
        e_shared: mov edi,ebx; call shared
        conv:     mov edi,ebx; call post; pop rbx; ret
        cond_a/cond_b/cond_c: xor eax,eax; ret    body_a/shared/post: ret

    Asserts: shared( appears three times over both passes (two copies, then
    one), each pass prints the goto and its label once, and only the default
    pass logs the merge.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000">
5389f383ff017417e83400000085c07405e83400000089dfe82e000000eb19e8
2000000085c07409e81a00000085c075d789dfe81300000089dfe80d0000005b
c331c0c331c0c331c0c3c3c3c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="g"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100041" name="cond_a"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100044" name="cond_b"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100047" name="cond_c"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x10004a" name="body_a"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x10004b" name="shared"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x10004c" name="post"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option dedupitetail off</com>
  <com>lo fu g</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option dedupitetail on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="shared(y) is printed once per arm, then once after the if" min="3" max="3">shared\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="each pass jumps into the true arm" min="2" max="2">goto label_100008;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="each pass prints that label" min="2" max="2">label_100008:</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="only the default pass merges the tail" min="1" max="1">// ite-dedupe</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="post(y) runs once per pass" min="2" max="2">post\(</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
